<SCRIPT LANGUAGE="JavaScript">

<!--//

   if (document.images) {

      // Load images needed [BACK] button.

      back_on  = new Image(); back_on.src  = "../../buttons/back_on.gif";  
      back_off = new Image(); back_off.src = "../../buttons/back.gif";  
   }

   function TurnOn() {

      // Displays image and updates status bar.

      if (document.images) {
         document["back"].src = back_on.src;
         window.status = 'Go back to previous page';
      }
   }

   function TurnOff() {

      // Displays image and clears status bar.

      if (document.images) {
         document["back"].src = back_off.src;
         window.status = '';
      }
   }

//-->

</SCRIPT>
<H3><CENTER><FONT COLOR="#ffff00"><A HREF="mailto:robbie.keyworth@uk.dreamcast.com">Robbie Keyworth</A></FONT></CENTER></H3>


        Robbie has a 93 'K' registration Silver 5dr Tipo 16V which he has owned for
	around 3 years. The car has been fabulous for most of this until the
	balancer shaft belt snapped fouling the cambelt and taking all 16 valves
	out. The engine had done 90,000 miles so he bought a complete
	1991 Thema 16v Turbo engine and he currently in the process of converting.
	<P>
	A word of advice to anyone considering a turbo transplant. Use a Coupe's.
	The Thema and Delta use completely different engine mounts to the front
	and rear of both engine and gearbox and it's not a straight swap.

